      "message": "IMO we could insert the check into the configuration parsing code which is run when EM starts. That way there is no need to potentially check this in other places and we can handle it at startup (fail-fast pattern).\n\nDo you agree with this or is there a reason we are checking it at a later point?\n\nWe could extract the map `typeToInterface` to be accessible from the configuration parsing code as well and simply check if the key exists. Otherwise drop the config with an error and all the rest of the code can simply assume the config type is supported and the key exists.",
