      "writtenOn": "2026-09-23T09:47:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just to make sure I\u0027m understanding the implications correctly: `typeToInterface` currently decides which Types get a declared `Item.\u003cType\u003e` interface, not which Types are accepted at all. An unlisted Type (e.g. Dimm) still gets a D-Bus object today, just without a dedicated interface.\n\nIf this table were also used as the parsing-stage validity gate, every schema-valid Type would need to be listed in it, whether or not it needs its own interface. Otherwise Dimm would go from \"object created without an interface\" to \"config rejected and dropped\" as a side effect.\n\nIf I\u0027m understanding correctly, that would effectively make this table the source of truth for accepted Types rather than just interface creation.",
      "parentUuid": "83f46c72_18a6084e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 166,
        "startChar": 54,
        "endLine": 171,
        "endChar": 77
      },
