      "writtenOn": "2026-09-18T16:15:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "sanitize implies they may be changed. Why do we need to use a changed config type for a D-Bus path?\n\nAll the config types supported by the schema are already safe for D-Bus. Using a config type not supported by the schema or not D-Bus-path-safe is not an intended use-case.\n\nThus there is no need to sanitize but only to check the value?\n\nA sanitized string here would contain `_` and fail to lookup in `typeToInterface` map.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 426,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 426,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "8351410b6d96a0d323468c620c69020aa93e56c4",
