      "writtenOn": "2026-09-23T09:47:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That makes sense.\n\nMy understanding is that sanitize here is acting more as a fallback for invalid input than as part of the intended Type model. Its primary purpose seems to be preventing an already-accepted Type value from producing an invalid D-Bus object path segment.\n\nIf Type is validated during configuration parsing as suggested above, then invalid values should never reach this path construction code in the first place. In that case, sanitize no longer appears to provide additional protection and could likely be removed as part of the same change.",
